"GM_STORIES":[{"t":"Um dia na praia","start":"Last Saturday, Ana and her friends decided to go to the beach.","steps":[["They took the bus because the car was broken.","They taked the bus because the car was broken.","They take the bus because the car was broken yesterday.","O passado de take é took (irregular)."],["When they arrived, the sun was shining.","When they arrive, the sun was shining.","When they arrived, the sun were shining.","Contando algo passado, use arrived; e the sun combina com was."],["Ana forgot her sunscreen, so she bought some.","Ana forgetted her sunscreen, so she buyed some.","Ana forgot her sunscreen, so she buy some.","Forget → forgot e buy → bought são irregulares."],["They swam for two hours and then ate sandwiches.","They swimmed for two hours and then ate sandwiches.","They swam for two hours and then eaten sandwiches.","Swim → swam e eat → ate no passado simples."],["It was the best day of the summer.","It was the most good day of the summer.","It were the best day of the summer.","O superlativo de good é the best; e it combina com was."]]},{"t":"O celular perdido","start":"Carlos woke up late and could not find his phone.","steps":[["He looked under the bed, but it wasn't there.","He looked under the bed, but it weren't there.","He look under the bed, but it wasn't there.","No passado, look vira looked; e it combina com wasn't."],["His sister said she had seen it in the kitchen.","His sister said she has saw it in the kitchen.","His sister said she seen it in the kitchen.","Had seen é o past perfect: had + particípio (seen)."],["He ran downstairs and found it next to the coffee.","He runned downstairs and found it next to the coffee.","He ran downstairs and finded it next to the coffee.","Run → ran e find → found são irregulares."],["The battery was almost dead, so he plugged it in.","The battery was almost died, so he plugged it in.","The battery was almost dead, so he plug it in.","Dead é adjetivo (\"sem vida\"); e o passado de plug é plugged."],["From that day on, he always leaves it in the same place.","From that day on, he always leave it in the same place.","From that day on, he always leaves it on the same place.","He + verbo com -s (leaves); e dizemos in the same place."]]},{"t":"A entrevista de emprego","start":"Marina had a job interview at nine o'clock.","steps":[["She woke up early and chose her best clothes.","She woked up early and chose her best clothes.","She woke up early and choosed her best clothes.","Wake → woke e choose → chose são irregulares."],["The office was far, so she left home an hour before.","The office was far, so she left home since an hour.","The office was far, so she leaved home an hour before.","O passado de leave é left; e usamos an hour before, não since."],["The manager asked her about her experience.","The manager asked to her about her experience.","The manager made her a question about her experience.","Ask não leva to; e \"fazer uma pergunta\" é ask a question (não make)."],["She answered every question with confidence.","She answered every question with confident.","She answer every question with confidence.","Depois de with usamos o substantivo (confidence); e o passado é answered."],["Two days later, they called her with great news.","Two days ago later, they called her with great news.","Two days later, they calling her with great news.","Two days later (depois); ago é \"atrás\". E o passado é called."]]},{"t":"Um fim de semana de chuva","start":"It was raining all weekend, so Tom stayed at home.","steps":[["He didn't have anything to do, so he started to read a book.","He didn't had anything to do, so he started to read a book.","He hasn't nothing to do, so he started to read a book.","Depois de didn't o verbo volta à forma base: have."],["The book was so interesting that he couldn't stop reading.","The book was so interested that he couldn't stop reading.","The book was too much interesting that he couldn't stop reading.","Interesting descreve a coisa; interested descreve a pessoa."],["Later, his friends invited him to play video games online.","Later, his friends invited him for play video games online.","Later, his friends invite him to play video games online.","Invite someone to + verbo; e o passado é invited."],["They played until midnight and laughed a lot.","They played until the midnight and laughed a lot.","They played until midnight and laugh a lot.","Dizemos until midnight (sem the); e laugh vira laughed no passado."],["On Monday, he felt tired but happy.","On Monday, he felt tiredly but happy.","In Monday, he felt tired but happy.","Depois de felt usamos adjetivo (tired); e dias da semana usam on."]]}],
